# Module Seed (mandatory)

When adding a **new collection module** under `src/<plural>/` (e.g. `products`, `brands`), always ship seed data in the same change.

Skip seed only for non-collection areas (`auth`, `profile`) unless the user asks.

## Checklist (same PR / same task)

1. Add `seedX` array in `src/database/seed-data.ts`
2. Insert loop in `src/database/seed.ts` (skip if unique key exists)
3. Delete in `src/database/clear.ts` via `deleteMany`
4. Use the Mongoose model via `getModelToken(Schema.name)` — same pattern as users/categories

## Patterns

```typescript
// seed-data.ts
export const seedProducts = [
  { name: 'Sample', price: 100, /* … */ },
];

// seed.ts — after users/categories loops
for (const item of seedProducts) {
  const exists = await productModel.exists({ name: item.name }); // unique field
  if (exists) {
    console.log(`Skipped product (exists): ${item.name}`);
    continue;
  }
  await productModel.create(item);
  console.log(`Created product: ${item.name}`);
}

// clear.ts
const productsResult = await productModel.deleteMany({});
console.log(`Deleted ${productsResult.deletedCount} product(s)`);
```

## Rules

- Seed must be **idempotent** (safe to re-run; skip duplicates)
- Prefer realistic sample fields that pass DTO/schema validation
- Images: use external `https://…` URLs in seed data (no file upload in seed scripts)
- Do not invent a second seed runner — extend `npm run seed` / `npm run seed:clear` only
- Completing a new CRUD module without seed is **incomplete**
